+++ b/docs/mobile-notifications-integration.md
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+# Mobile shared in-app notifications (phase 6)
+
+Apply `mobile-v4.patch`, `mobile-claims.patch`, then `mobile-notifications.patch` to backend `42b4552`. Run Prisma generate and migrate deploy against a separate development/test database first. The new migration only adds nullable `message_bs` and `read_at` columns to the existing notifications table. It does not reset data or alter staff SMS delivery state. No new dependency is required.
+
+## Routes
+
+- `GET /api/v1/mobile/beneficiaries/me/notifications` returns only the signed-in beneficiary's IN_APP messages, with SENT/READ status and a nonfuture sentAt. A linked schedule must belong to that beneficiary. The DTO is `id`, `scheduleId`, `title`, `titleBs`, `message`, `messageBs`, `notificationType`, `sentAt`, `readAt`; all timestamps are ISO UTC. No delivery internals, staff IDs, recipient details, provider references, QR secrets or evidence are returned. Titles and categories derive from controlled event types. Existing custom IN_APP messages use an Account update title and their saved text.
+- `PATCH /api/v1/mobile/beneficiaries/me/notifications/:notificationId/read` sets the first read time using an ownership/visibility-scoped conditional update, then returns `id` and `readAt`. Retried/concurrent reads preserve that time. Missing, foreign and invisible records return 404. Staff JWTs are rejected by beneficiary authentication. Both routes return private/no-store.
+
+## Automatic staff events
+
+In-app rows are inserted in the same database transaction as enrollment review/correction/approval/rejection, distribution publication, final QR/biometric/signature verification, physical release, and simulated benefit credit/reversal. Partial identity checks do not announce completion. Draft schedule edits and draft cancellation are unpublished and produce no alerts. The existing staff rules lock schedule edits and reject event cancellation after opening; this phase does not change those rules.
+
+Rows use controlled English/Bisaya messages and stable hashed event keys with ON CONFLICT skipping duplicates. Business rollback also removes the new alert. Verification/release/credit idempotency replays do not duplicate messages. Published assignments are inserted in a batch. No existing event is replayed/backfilled during migration. Staff notes, release evidence, biometric/signature data and raw QR values are never copied into message text. Simulated ledger notices explicitly state that no real funds moved.
+
+These rows use IN_APP/SENT and provider mode IN_APP. They do not enter the SMS queue or need Redis, a worker, Expo push or an SMS provider. Delivery preference switches remain previews. The mobile app refreshes on opening Notifications and offers manual refresh; background push/realtime delivery is separate work.
+
+## Verification
+
+From mobile, run `npm.cmd test`, `npm.cmd run typecheck` and `npm.cmd run test:shared` with DATABASE_URL pointing to the migrated isolated test instance. The actual client/API test covers staff-created updates, no draft alerts (including draft cancellation), final versus partial verification, release/credit/reversal replay, publication, owner and linked-schedule isolation, delivery-channel/status/time filtering, DTO allowlists, first-read races, a later login, invalid IDs, authentication/logout and transaction rollback. Settlement prerequisites are synthetic; live biometrics and real funds are not exercised.
+
+The backend's existing verification-time fixtures also check that combined methods announce verification only after completion and that replay/duplicate scans preserve one alert. Run backend `npm.cmd test` for regression checks.
+
+For manual testing, have authorized staff perform a new enrollment decision, publish a test assignment or release test assistance. In mobile, open Notifications and refresh, open a message and return to confirm its unread dot disappears, then sign out/in to confirm that read state remains saved. Existing pre-migration test releases do not create new alerts by themselves. No production or hosted backend has been changed by this local implementation.
